 "mechanism": "MULTIMODAL, not flat: every theta combination is LOCALLY informative (FIM eigenvalues 1641-3579279 >> prior precision 16) because log|H| has huge gradients near resonances; but many distinct theta align different subsets of the dense resonances comparably well, so the GLOBAL posterior has many sharp modes separated by high barriers. Single-chain NUTS gets trapped one mode per chain (R-hat 29-360, ESS~2 across arm-B folds). This is the ridged/multimodal regime the compute protocol names for TMCMC; per AGENTS it is reported as a non-converged, multimodal posterior (many theta fit comparably in data space), NOT a sampler bug and NOT under-identification-by-insensitivity."
